      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day, which is about twice the maximum labeled daily dose of metformin. The maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, usually given as 850 mg three times daily. A dose this high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nWas this a typo? Possible intended orders include:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **500 mg PO three times daily with meals** (1,500 mg/day)\n- **1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals** (2,000 mg/day)\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, divided in some other way\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it. If you really do want 1700 mg three times daily, please confirm that explicitly and I'll enter it with a note documenting that it was intentional. I'd suggest checking it with pharmacy first."
      }
